{
  "id": "fluency-l8-adding-forever",
  "lesson": "l8-adding-forever",
  "title": "Fluency: sums to infinity",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "from-the-terms",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "find a sum to infinity from the terms",
      "vars": {
        "p": { "int": [1, 4] },
        "j": { "int": [1, 3] },
        "g": { "pick": [1, -1] },
        "m": { "int": [1, 3] },
        "s": { "pick": [1, -1] }
      },
      "let": {
        "q": "p + j", "r": "g*p/(p + j)",
        "a": "s*m*q^2", "t2": "s*m*g*p*q", "t3": "s*m*p^2",
        "om": "1 - r",
        "sum": "a/(1 - r)",
        "plus": "a/(1 + r)",
        "noa": "1/(1 - r)"
      },
      "where": ["gcd(p, j) == 1", "q <= 5", "abs(sum) <= 200", "abs(noa - sum) > 0.02", "abs(noa - plus) > 0.02", "abs(plus - sum) > 0.02"],
      "prompt": "Find $S_\\infty$ for ${a}{t2:+}{t3:+} + \\dots$ Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{sum}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "placeholder": "A fraction or a decimal" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "sign-of-r", "value": "{plus}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "line": "You divided by $1 + r$. The rule is $\\dfrac{{a}}{{1 - r}}$, and here $r = {r:frac}$." },
        { "id": "first-term-left-out", "value": "{noa}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "line": "You worked out $\\dfrac{{1}}{{1 - r}}$. Multiply it by the first term, {a}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Here $a = {a}$ and $r = {t2} \\div {a:()} = {r:frac}$, so $|r| < 1$.",
        "$1 - r = {om:frac}$.",
        "So $S_\\infty = {a:()} \\div {om:frac} = {sum:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "from-a-and-r",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "find a sum to infinity from a and r",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-20, 30], "not": [0, 1] },
        "p": { "int": [1, 4] },
        "j": { "int": [1, 4] },
        "g": { "pick": [1, -1] }
      },
      "let": {
        "r": "g*p/(p + j)", "om": "1 - r",
        "sum": "a/(1 - r)",
        "plus": "a/(1 + r)",
        "noa": "1/(1 - r)"
      },
      "where": ["gcd(p, j) == 1", "p + j <= 5", "abs(noa - sum) > 0.02", "abs(noa - plus) > 0.02", "abs(plus - sum) > 0.02"],
      "prompt": "A geometric series has first term {a} and common ratio ${r:frac}$. What is $S_\\infty$? Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{sum}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "placeholder": "A fraction or a decimal" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "sign-of-r", "value": "{plus}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "line": "You divided by $1 + r$. The rule is $\\dfrac{{a}}{{1 - r}}$, and here $r = {r:frac}$." },
        { "id": "first-term-left-out", "value": "{noa}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "line": "You worked out $\\dfrac{{1}}{{1 - r}}$. Multiply it by the first term, {a}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "$|r| < 1$, so the sum to infinity exists.",
        "$1 - r = {om:frac}$.",
        "So $S_\\infty = {a:()} \\div {om:frac} = {sum:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "perpetual-bond",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "value a payment that lasts forever",
      "vars": {
        "c": { "pick": [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 15, 20, 25, 30] },
        "i": { "pick": [2, 2.5, 4, 5, 8, 10] }
      },
      "let": { "g": "1 + i/100", "ir": "i/100", "val": "c/(i/100)", "now": "c/(i/100) + c", "pct": "c/i" },
      "where": ["val < 1000"],
      "prompt": "A perpetual bond pays £{c:dp2} at the end of every year, forever. With {i}% interest, a payment in $k$ years is worth $\\tfrac{{{c}}}{{{g}^k}}$ pounds today. What is the bond worth today?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{val}", "tol": { "abs": 0.005 }, "unit": "£", "placeholder": "Pounds" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "payment-today", "value": "{now}", "line": "You counted a payment today. The first payment is a year away, so the first term is $\\tfrac{{{c}}}{{{g}}}$." },
        { "id": "per-cent-not-decimal", "value": "{pct}", "line": "You divided by {i}. The rate is {i}%, which is {ir} as a decimal." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The first term is $\\tfrac{{{c}}}{{{g}}}$ and the ratio is $\\tfrac{{1}}{{{g}}}$.",
        "So $S_\\infty = \\dfrac{{{c}/{g}}}{{1 - 1/{g}}} = \\dfrac{{{c}}}{{{ir}}}$.",
        "The bond is worth £{val:dp2}."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
